  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung listens and asks his sons.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Tell your old father what I have heard you are always talking about and what business you have in the town.\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"We are setting up a great grain market and we have bought a good deal of grain and we have hired men and we have bought a good plot of land for a market and we have a big house for it.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) They are setting up a grain market for the sons.",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his dislike for the market.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"I do not like markets,\"",
  "[action] The eldest son and the second son are silent.",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his dislike for the market.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"I have enough for my own house and for my slaves and I am content.\"",
  "[action] The eldest son and the second son are silent.",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits on his bed.",
  "[action] Wang Lung watches the two sons, content.",
  "[action] Wang Lung observes the two sons.",
